  "vysu": "# title: Precession Explorer\n# version: 2\n# featured: true\n# group: Precession\n# tags: pole-track, top-view, thuban, polaris\n# order: 30\n# Top-down review of precession against the fixed nakshatra ring.\n\n# --- SECTION 1: Initialization & Staging ---\n# Transition to immersive mode and set the starting era.\ntheater\nstage blank night year -4000\ncamera pos 0,325,0.1 target 0,0,0 fov 42\n\ncaption \"Precession and Pole Star\" 2000:300:450\n\n# --- SECTION 2: Celestial Landscape Build-up ---\n# Gradually reveal the stars and the nakshatra (asterism) line art.\nrollout stars 5000:\nrollout naks 5000:\nhide stars\nhide naks\n\n# Highlight the Ecliptic Band with its 27 segments.\nrollout eclipticNakSegments 5000:\nrollout stars 1000:\nrollout naks 1000:\n\n# Reveal mythical polar constellations (Shishumara and Matsya Dhruva).\nrollout sisumara 3000:\nrollout matsya 3000:\n\n# Set up polar reference markers.\nshow northPolarItems \nhide southPolarItems\nshow poleTrack # The circle traced by the Earth's axis over ~26,000 years.\n\nshow NP; # Current North Pole marker.\nshow seasonalFrame # The Equator and Equinox/Solstice markers.\n\nflash precessionCircle 1500:\n\n# --- SECTION 3: The Drift of Time (Pole Star Transition) ---\ncaption \"The pole marker drifts as centuries pass\" 3000:350:500\n\nflash NP 2000:\nflash seasonalFrame 2000:\n\nshow overlay # Show the time/coordinate HUD.\n\n# Animation: 4000 BCE to 2800 BCE.\ntravel -4000 to -2800 7000: step 100\ncaption \"Thuban becomes the north-pole marker near 2800 BCE\" 5000:1000:500\nflash NP 2000:; hide NP; wait 1000; flash NP 2000:\n\n# Animation: 2800 BCE to 2100 CE.\ntravel -2800 to 2100 15000: step 100\ncaption \"Polaris becomes the north-pole marker near 2100 CE\" 5000:1000:500\nflash NP 2000:; hide NP; wait 1000; flash NP 2000:\n\nwait 5000\n\n# --- SECTION 4: Perspective View Exploration ---\n# Reset camera to a 3D perspective to see the tilt of the axis.\nstage blank night year -4000\ncamera pos -147.464,73.504,234.757 target 0,0,0 fov 45\n\ncaption \"Visualize Precession\" 1200:250:350\n \nrollout stars 5000:\nrollout naks 5000:\nhide eclipticGrid\ngrid equatorial 10 red\nrollout equatorialGrid 5000:\nstyle nsAxis yellow\nrollout nsAxis 2000: # North-South physical axis of Earth.\nflash nsAxis\nwait 500\nshow eclipticNakSegments 3000:\nshow seasonalFrame\nflash seasonalFrame\nflash AE; hide AE; show AE; flash AE # Autumnal Equinox.\nflash SS; hide SS; show SS; flash SS # Summer Solstice.\nflash VE; hide VE; show VE; flash VE # Vernal Equinox.\nflash WS; hide WS; show WS; flash WS # Winter Solstice.\nshow poleTrack\n\nshow overlay\n# Repeat time drift in perspective view.\ntravel -4000 to -2800 7000: step 100\ncaption \"Thuban becomes the north-pole marker near 2800 BCE\" 5000:1000:500\nflash NP 2000:; hide NP; wait 1000; flash NP 2000:\n\ntravel -2800 to 2100 15000: step 100\ncaption \"Polaris becomes the north-pole marker near 2100 CE\" 5000:1000:500\nflash NP 2000:; hide NP; wait 1000; flash NP 2000:\n\nwait 5000\n\n# Exit theater mode and return to interactive canvas.\ncanvas\n",
